From: FunnyPlaying RetroPixel Pocket port
Subject: [PATCH] cmd/hwrev: recognize FunnyPlaying RetroPixel Pocket

On RK3326 handhelds the Hardkernel-descended u-boot-legacy reads
SARADC channel 0 during board identification and maps the raw value to
one of a small hard-coded list of known devices (Odroid GO 2/3,
Anbernic RG351V, Gameconsole R33S, ...).  If the value doesn't
match any known range it falls through to an 'engineer sample'
default that sets dtb_name="rk3326-odroidgo2-linux.dtb" — a file
not shipped by ROCKNIX under that exact name, so fatload fails
and the board bails out with odroid_alert_leds().

The RetroPixel Pocket returns an ADC reading of ~399 on channel 0
(measured from userspace via /sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:device0/
in_voltage0_raw after the kernel boots).  Add a matching branch.

---
 cmd/hwrev.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cmd/hwrev.c b/cmd/hwrev.c
--- a/cmd/hwrev.c
+++ b/cmd/hwrev.c
@@ -54,6 +54,11 @@ int do_hwrev(cmd_tbl_t *cmdtp, int flag, int argc, char * const argv[])
         else if (check_range(460, 489, hwrev_adc)) {
                 env_set("hwrev", "chi");
                 env_set("dtb_name", "rk3326-gameforce-chi.dtb");
         }
+	/* FunnyPlaying RetroPixel Pocket (RK3326) */
+	else if (check_range(380, 420, hwrev_adc)) {
+		env_set("hwrev", "rppocket");
+		env_set("dtb_name", "rk3326-funnyplaying-rppocket.dtb");
+	}
 	/* engineer samples */
 	else {
 		env_set("hwrev", "v00");
